@page "/packages"
<PageTitle>NuGet Packages // The Singularity Workshop</PageTitle>

<section class="catalog">
    <header class="catalog__header">
        <p class="catalog__eyebrow">THE WORKSHOP // PACKAGE INDEX</p>
        <h1>NuGet packages</h1>
        <p>Discover reusable .NET capabilities, then follow each package back to its source, documentation, and release evidence. A package is listed here as published only when its NuGet listing is verified.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="catalog__grid">
        <article class="catalog__card">
            <span class="catalog__kind">STATE RUNTIME</span>
            <h2>FSM_API</h2>
            <p>The engine-agnostic finite-state-machine core.</p>
            <a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/TheSingularityWorkshop.FSM_API">View on NuGet ↗</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/FSM_API">Source repository ↗</a>
        </article>
        <article class="catalog__card">
            <span class="catalog__kind">AI INTEROPERABILITY</span>
            <h2>ProtocolAi</h2>
            <p>Integer-backed vocabulary and protocol payload structures. Current development work is pre-release.</p>
            <a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.ProtocolAi">Source and release status ↗</a>
        </article>
        <article class="catalog__card">
            <span class="catalog__kind">AI STRUCTURE</span>
            <h2>GrammarAi</h2>
            <p>Immutable grammar definitions that reference protocol symbols. Current development work is pre-release.</p>
            <a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.GrammarAi">Source and release status ↗</a>
        </article>
        <article class="catalog__card">
            <span class="catalog__kind">AI PROVIDER ADAPTERS</span>
            <h2>HeadlessAi</h2>
            <p>Headless provider adapters with host-controlled security boundaries. Current development work is pre-release.</p>
            <a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.HeadlessAi">Source and release status ↗</a>
        </article>
    </div>

    <p class="catalog__note">This first pass intentionally separates a verified published listing from repositories under release preparation. It is not yet a complete inventory of the Workshop’s 15+ package IDs; the remaining entries should be filled from actual project/package metadata and checked against NuGet before they are labelled published.</p>
    <nav class="catalog__crosslinks" aria-label="Related catalogs">
        <a href="/repositories">Browse source repositories →</a>
        <a href="/">Return to the Workshop →</a>
    </nav>
</section>

<style>
.catalog{max-width:1200px;margin:0 auto;padding:clamp(1rem,4vw,3rem);color:#e7f2fb;background:radial-gradient(ellipse at 50% 0,rgba(255,44,255,.07),transparent 45%),#030812;min-height:100%}
.catalog__header{max-width:780px;margin:0 auto 2rem}.catalog__eyebrow,.catalog__kind{font:700 .7rem Consolas,monospace;letter-spacing:.16em;color:#00eaff}.catalog__header h1{font-size:clamp(2.5rem,7vw,5rem);line-height:1;margin:.5rem 0 1rem;color:white}.catalog__header p:last-child{line-height:1.7;color:#a6bacb}
.catalog__grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,260px),1fr));gap:1rem}.catalog__card{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start;gap:.65rem;padding:1.25rem;background:rgba(5,15,29,.92);border:1px solid rgba(0,234,255,.2);min-height:205px}.catalog__card h2{font-size:1.45rem;color:white;margin:0}.catalog__card p{color:#a6bacb;line-height:1.6;margin:0 0 .4rem;flex:1}.catalog a{color:#69dfff;text-underline-offset:.2em}.catalog a:hover{color:#ff8df5}.catalog__note{margin:1.5rem 0;color:#9db0c2;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6}.catalog__crosslinks{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1.2rem;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,234,255,.2);padding-top:1.2rem}
</style>
